# What must NOT be sent to the daemon when building the image.
#
# Without this file `docker compose up --build` sends the whole directory, which
# is 7.9 GB, 7.6 of it in dist/ (built bundles and kits). The build does not
# fail, it just drags on for minutes for no reason, and the promise of "up and
# running in five minutes" stops being true before Docker even gets to pip.
#
# The rule is simple: source code and what is built from it go into the context.
# Data, build artefacts and the local environment do not.

# ── Build and delivery artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.whl

# ── Live data: database, uploads, perf logs, backups ──────────────────────
# Mounted as a volume (./data:/data); they have no business inside the image,
# and this is the only way they could leak into an image layer.
data/
backups/

# ── Local developer environment ───────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Vendored engine assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~150 MB, downloaded by deploy/fetch-*.py. They reach the image not via this
# context but as the named build context `engine-assets` that
# deploy/make-bundle.sh passes (see the Dockerfile); the dev profile loads
# Pyodide from the CDN.
static/pyodide/
static/duckdb-wasm/
static/duckdb-ext/
static/arrow-esm/
static/xlsx-arrow/
engine/xlsx-arrow/target/

# ── History and housekeeping ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.claude/
scratchpad/
scratch-ui/
*.log
.DS_Store

# ── Tests and developer tools ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not executed inside the image; excluded for context size, not for secrecy.
tests/
docs/
